      "content": "It's incredibly draining when the perceived reality is that you are trapped within a relentless cycle of obligations. Feeling trapped by debt and expectations makes the pressure unbearable, turning daily life into a performance under intense scrutiny. Sometimes, instead of seeking a massive change, focusing on micro-adjustments to create tiny pockets of relief can help lessen the immediate strain. Remember that the way you perceive the ending of the script is within your control, even if the challenging plot remains.",
      "source": "target",
